node_modules
dist
storybook-static
.nx
*.log
.DS_Store

# undrift hook scratch state (attempt counters). Decisions are NOT scratch:
# undrift.decisions.json is committed on purpose.
.undrift/

# assess fixture subjects are trimmed extracts of REAL design systems, and the
# parts that matter live in directories the rules above ignore: the vendored
# fixture is all `dist/` (its entry .d.ts and its stylesheet, the token source),
# and the source-only fixtures need a minimal `node_modules` or the TypeScript
# checker cannot resolve a single component. Without these negations `git add`
# drops them silently and the suite only passes on the machine that built it.
!packages/undrift/tests/corpus/subjects/**

# …but junk inside the negated fixture tree stays ignored. The negation above
# re-includes EVERYTHING under subjects/, which would otherwise let .DS_Store
# or a stray .undrift/ scratch dir (assess runs against these very subjects)
# ride into a `git add -A`.
packages/undrift/tests/corpus/subjects/**/.DS_Store
packages/undrift/tests/corpus/subjects/**/*.log
packages/undrift/tests/corpus/subjects/**/.undrift/
